course: dictionary
lesson: 14612
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning separately, and you choose the one that fits the sentence. The word popper can mean a party toy, a fastener on clothes, a popcorn machine, or anything that pops.
explain: «At the party, we pulled a popper and paper streamers flew over the table.» Here popper means a party popper, the paper tube that goes bang. The words party and streamers are the clues. Always look at the words around the word first.
explain: «Mum did up the poppers on the baby's jumpsuit.» In the UK, poppers can be press studs, the small snap fasteners on clothes. The words did up and jumpsuit show which meaning fits. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have probably got it.
fact: A party popper is a small paper tube that goes bang and shoots out curly streamers when you pull its string.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, a popper is a press stud: a small fastener in two halves that snap together on clothes.
fact: A popcorn popper is a machine or pan that makes popcorn.
fact: Anything that pops can be called a popper, such as a fishing lure that pops on the water.
fact: Many words have several meanings, so always check the clues in the sentence.
exercise: «At the birthday party, we pulled a popper and curly streamers flew everywhere.» What does popper mean here? | A bird that pops up from the grass | A type of cake | A pan for cooking corn | *A party popper that goes bang
exercise: «Jack could not do up the poppers on his coat because his fingers were cold.» What are poppers in this sentence? | Small paper streamers | Machines for making popcorn | Fishing lures | *Press studs that snap together on clothes
exercise: «The popcorn popper was full of hot, fluffy corn.» What is a popcorn popper? | A type of fishing rod | *A machine or pan for making popcorn | A bag of sweets | A paper hat
test: «The lure was a popper, and it bounced on the water to catch the fish.» What does popper mean here? | A press stud on a jacket | A snack from a bag | A party streamer | *Anything that pops, like a fishing lure
test: Tom says popper has only one meaning. Is he right? | *No, popper has several meanings, so check the sentence | Yes, because it is a noun | Yes, it only ever means a party toy | No, it means a fast runner
exam: Which sentence uses popper to mean a press stud? | «The popper bounced on the water.» | *«The popper on my coat came undone.» | «The popper went bang at the party.» | «The popper made hot popcorn for the film.»
